{"name":"Dinosaur Egg","hex":"#cabaa9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dinosaur","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Those animals of the clade Dinosauria that existed during the Triassic, Jurassic and Cretaceous periods and are now extinct. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Any of the animals belonging to the clade Dinosauria, including its sole surviving lineage: Neornithes."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very old or old-fashioned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dinosaur"},{"term":"egg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food.","An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something).","To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dinosaur egg","blocks":[{"text":"Dinosaur eggs are the organic vessels in which a dinosaur embryo develops. When the first scientifically documented remains of non-avian dinosaurs were being described in England during the 1820s, it was presumed that dinosaurs had laid eggs because they were reptiles. In 1859, the first scientifically documented dinosaur egg fossils were discovered in France by Jean-Jacques Pouech, although they were mistaken for giant bird eggs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Indroda_eggs.JPG/330px-Indroda_eggs.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dinosaur_egg","wikidata":"Q3817122"},{"title":"Dinosaur","blocks":[{"text":"Dinosaurs are a diverse group of warmblooded reptiles of the clade Dinosauria. They existed through most of the Mesozoic era, first appearing early in the Triassic period. They became the dominant terrestrial vertebrates after the Triassic–Jurassic extinction event 201.3 mya and their dominance continued throughout the Jurassic and Cretaceous periods. The fossil record shows that birds are feathered dinosaurs, having evolved from earlier theropods during the Late Jurassic epoch, and are the only dinosaur lineage known to have survived the Cretaceous–Paleogene extinction event approximately 66 mya. Dinosaurs can therefore be divided into avian dinosaurs—birds—and the extinct non-avian dinosaurs, which are all dinosaurs other than birds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Sinosauropteryxfossil.jpg/330px-Sinosauropteryxfossil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dinosaur","wikidata":"Q430"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg","wikidata":"Q17147"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Citipati_embryo.jpg/500px-Citipati_embryo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Citipati_embryo.jpg/500px-Citipati_embryo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Citipati osmolskae egg with preserved embryo, at the AMNH.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACitipati_embryo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Zkamen%C4%9Bl%C3%A9_vejce_dinosaura_z_pou%C5%A1t%C4%9B_Gobi%2C_expozice_N%C3%A1rodn%C3%ADho_muzea_v_Praze_%282007%29.jpg/500px-Zkamen%C4%9Bl%C3%A9_vejce_dinosaura_z_pou%C5%A1t%C4%9B_Gobi%2C_expozice_N%C3%A1rodn%C3%ADho_muzea_v_Praze_%282007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Zkamen%C4%9Bl%C3%A9_vejce_dinosaura_z_pou%C5%A1t%C4%9B_Gobi%2C_expozice_N%C3%A1rodn%C3%ADho_muzea_v_Praze_%282007%29.jpg/1280px-Zkamen%C4%9Bl%C3%A9_vejce_dinosaura_z_pou%C5%A1t%C4%9B_Gobi%2C_expozice_N%C3%A1rodn%C3%ADho_muzea_v_Praze_%282007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Zkamen%C4%9Bl%C3%A9_vejce_dinosaura_z_pou%C5%A1t%C4%9B_Gobi%2C_expozice_N%C3%A1rodn%C3%ADho_muzea_v_Praze_%282007%29.jpg/500px-Zkamen%C4%9Bl%C3%A9_vejce_dinosaura_z_pou%C5%A1t%C4%9B_Gobi%2C_expozice_N%C3%A1rodn%C3%ADho_muzea_v_Praze_%282007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fossilized dinosaur egg from the Gobi Desert, National Museum in Prague","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZkamen%C4%9Bl%C3%A9_vejce_dinosaura_z_pou%C5%A1t%C4%9B_Gobi%2C_expozice_N%C3%A1rodn%C3%ADho_muzea_v_Praze_(2007).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia